Description: Provides general-purpose data profiling and quality analysis for
    tabular data. Discovers structural patterns, implicit types, mixed date
    formats and reusable findings about potential data issues. Defines quality
    frameworks with user-declared dimensions and factors, reusable metrics with
    explicit granularity, typed aggregation, evaluation profiles, versioned
    histories, structural drift detection, and self-contained HyperText Markup
    Language reports without external rendering software.
    Produces editable cleaning plans and applies only explicitly selected
    actions while retaining an audit log. Includes bounded value distributions,
    quantiles, mixed-type associations,
    temporal regularity checks, and confirmable measurement-scale proposals.
    The general model follows the data-quality lineage described by Batini and
    Scannapieco (2016) <doi:10.1007/978-3-319-24106-7>. The package ships a
    traceable implementation of the Data Quality Management Framework for
    Digital Government, version 1.6, published by AGESIC (2020)
    <https://www.gub.uy/agencia-gobierno-electronico-sociedad-informacion-conocimiento/>,
    and an optional taxonomy of the fifteen characteristics in ISO/IEC
    25012:2008 <https://www.iso.org/standard/35736.html>.
